WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
Two parents both show the
same version of a feature.

2
00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:06.410
It's a feature controlled
by a single gene.

3
00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.570
Their child shows a different version,

4
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.730
one that neither parent has.

5
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.130
Nothing has mutated.

6
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.670
Nothing has been added.

7
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.390
So where did the child's
version come from?

8
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.770
In this mission, you'll meet alleles,

9
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.610
the different versions of a gene,

10
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.990
and find out why some are
dominant and some are recessive.

11
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.550
You'll learn the words
genotype and phenotype,

12
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.330
homozygous and heterozygous.

13
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.730
And you'll use a Punnett square
to predict the children of two

14
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:33.910
parents.

15
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.180
Your mission: explain how a
hidden feature can reappear.
